<section class="erp-doc-section" id="quickstart"><h2>Set up Betrio in 15 minutes</h2><p>This quick start takes a new business from an empty system to its first signed report.</p><ol><li><b>Check company settings:</b> open Administration → Settings and verify the business details.</li><li><b>Create employees:</b> create individual Nextcloud accounts for office staff and field workers and assign the appropriate groups.</li><li><b>Sign in once:</b> new employees sign in to Nextcloud once so they become available for Betrio permissions.</li><li><b>Assign permissions:</b> define who may administer Betrio and who may work from mobile devices.</li><li><b>Create customers:</b> create customer records or import existing Nextcloud contacts.</li><li><b>Create a project:</b> assign the customer, project name and responsible employees.</li><li><b>Set up mobile:</b> open Betrio Mobile on the field worker's phone and install it as an app.</li><li><b>On site:</b> record time, material, photos and documents against the project.</li><li><b>Report:</b> review the work, obtain the customer's signature and process the report in the office.</li></ol><div class="erp-doc-box"><b>Practical rule:</b> complete one full test job before enabling additional employees for production use.</div><div class="erp-doc-box"><b>Support diagnostics:</b> System Check can download a diagnostic report as a text file. It contains technical test results and suggested solutions, but intentionally excludes customer/project data, passwords and tokens.</div></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="company"><h2>Set up company</h2><div class="erp-doc-box"><b>New:</b> The initial setup wizard guides you through company details, users, basic settings, calendar, mobile and system checks. It can be reopened later under Administration → Settings.</div><p>After installation, enter your company master data first. Betrio uses this information for letterheads and report PDFs.</p><ol><li>Open <b>Administration → Settings</b>.</li><li>Under <b>Company data & letterhead</b>, enter the full company name.</li><li>Add owner or management, street, postal code, city and country.</li><li>Enter phone number, email address and website.</li><li>If required, enter tax number, VAT ID, registry court and registration number.</li><li>Upload the <b>company logo</b> as PNG or JPG.</li><li>Choose <b>Save company data</b>.</li><li>Create a test report and check the PDF.</li></ol><div class="erp-doc-box"><b>Important:</b> Verify company name, address, contact data and logo before creating the first production report.</div><h3>What appears on a report?</h3><p>The report uses the company logo and master data from Settings. Changes therefore only need to be maintained centrally.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="checklist"><h2>Setup checklist for a new business</h2><p>This sequence is recommended after a new installation or when setting up a new test system.</p><ol><li>Open System Check and verify the technical requirements.</li><li>Enter company details and company logo.</li><li>Check numbering sequences and business settings.</li><li>Check hourly rates and time evaluation settings.</li><li>Create Nextcloud users for office staff and field workers.</li><li>Assign users to the appropriate groups and verify Betrio permissions.</li><li>Select the team calendar or verify calendar integration.</li><li>Create a test customer or import one from Nextcloud Contacts.</li><li>Create a test project and assign it to a field worker.</li><li>Check document and photo access in the test project.</li><li>Record a test time entry and a material item.</li><li>Create a report, sign it and download it as a PDF.</li><li>Open Betrio Mobile on a mobile device and check camera/browser permissions.</li><li>Document the Nextcloud server's backup and update procedure.</li></ol><div class="erp-doc-box"><b>Ready for operation:</b> When this test works completely, the basic setup is complete.</div></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="start"><h2>1. Welcome to Betrio</h2><p>Betrio is an ERP system that runs directly in Nextcloud. Customers, projects, working time, materials, reports, documents and the mobile site view remain in one shared working environment.</p><h3>Quick start</h3><ol><li>Install and enable Betrio.</li><li>Check company data and settings.</li><li>Create Nextcloud users for office staff and field workers.</li><li>Create customers and projects.</li><li>Grant the responsible employees access to their projects.</li><li>Install the Betrio Mobile view on mobile devices.</li></ol></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="installation"><h2>2. Installation & requirements</h2><p>Betrio runs as a Nextcloud app. A working standard Nextcloud installation with a database, HTTPS and cron background jobs is required.</p><ol><li>Copy Betrio to the Nextcloud app directory.</li><li>Assign the files to the web-server user.</li><li>Enable Betrio in Nextcloud or run the upgrade.</li><li>Open <b>System Check</b> and verify that the required components are available.</li></ol><div class="erp-doc-box">HTTPS is required for the installable mobile web app.</div></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="setup"><h2>3. Initial setup</h2><p>Initial configuration is managed under <b>Administration → Settings</b>. This is where the master data and business defaults used by Betrio are maintained.</p><h3>Check before the first job</h3><ul><li><b>Company data & letterhead:</b> company name, address, contact details, tax/registry details and logo.</li><li><b>Numbering sequences:</b> verify numbering for customers, projects and reports.</li><li><b>Hourly rates:</b> check the basis used for internal evaluations.</li><li><b>Team calendar:</b> select the desired Nextcloud calendar.</li><li><b>Users & permissions:</b> assign suitable access to office users, administrators and field workers.</li><li><b>Mobile:</b> verify the mobile URL and device notes under Administration → Mobile.</li><li><b>System Check:</b> resolve technical warnings before production use.</li></ul></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="users"><h2>4. Users, employees & field workers</h2><p>Betrio uses Nextcloud accounts. Create the user in Nextcloud first; the user should sign in once before Betrio roles, access and hourly rates are assigned.</p><p>Use separate accounts for every person. Do not share credentials. Permissions determine which modules and projects are available to each user.</p><div class="erp-doc-box"><b>Tip:</b> Give users only the permissions required for their work. Administrative access should remain limited.</div></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="customers"><h2>5. Customer management</h2><p>The customer record combines contact details, projects, documents, CRM activity and follow-ups. Customers can be created manually or imported from supported Nextcloud contacts.</p><ul><li>Maintain postal and electronic contact details in one place.</li><li>Use customer numbers consistently.</li><li>Store invoice-specific fields such as routing ID, order reference, cost center or DATEV account where required.</li><li>Archive customers instead of deleting business history that is still required.</li></ul></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="projects"><h2>6. Projects</h2><p>Projects connect customers, employees, time entries, materials, reports, files and billing preparation. Create a project for every operational job that should be evaluated separately.</p><p>Assign responsible employees and keep project status and due dates current. Project access controls what field workers can see in Betrio Mobile.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="time"><h2>7. Time tracking</h2><p>Betrio separates <b>attendance time</b> from <b>project time</b>. The digital time clock records when an employee is actually present. Project timers and manual time entries assign working time to a project. The two values are intentionally independent.</p><p>Project time can be recorded by timer or afterwards with date, start, end, break and activity. Betrio calculates the project duration minus the break. A later project entry may therefore differ from attendance recorded on the same day.</p><div class="erp-doc-box"><b>Practical note:</b> A positive difference between attendance and project time is time not yet assigned to a project. If project time exceeds attendance, Betrio marks it as project time without attendance.</div></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="working-time-profile"><h2>Working-time profiles</h2><p>Under Employees, maintain target hours for each weekday, annual leave, the start date of the working-time account and any opening balance. The weekly target is calculated from the seven weekday values, supporting part-time models and different working days.</p><p>The <b>working-time account start date</b> is the cut-off date. Times before this date remain available as project time but are not included in target/actual calculations. The opening balance is added once to the calculated balance.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="attendance-clock"><h2>Digital time clock & attendance</h2><p>The time clock follows the sequence <b>Clock in → Break → Continue working → Clock out</b>. Breaks are deducted from attendance. Clock events are logged.</p><p>Administrators can add forgotten attendance manually. A manual attendance entry does not create project time. Manual attendance periods must not overlap existing clock events for the same employee.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="absence-time"><h2>Leave & absences</h2><p>Approved absences credit the target time configured for planned working days. Record the absence type and period and use the employee overview to monitor annual leave and days already taken.</p><p>Keep absence records separate from project time so project evaluations continue to represent productive project work.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="staff-planning"><h2>Staff planning</h2><p>The weekly staff-planning view assigns employees to jobs and dates. Use previous/next week navigation to plan upcoming work and coordinate field teams.</p><p>Planning does not replace actual time tracking. Planned assignments describe intended work; attendance and project time document what actually happened.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="working-time-account"><h2>Working-time account & target/actual</h2><p>The working-time account compares credited actual time with the employee's configured target. The opening balance and configured start date define the calculation period.</p><p>Use the time evaluation to review weekly hours, recorded times, absences and balances before payroll or internal reporting.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="material"><h2>8. Material & inventory</h2><p>The material master stores article data, groups, suppliers, purchase prices, sales calculations, stock quantities and storage locations. Inventory movements remain traceable.</p><ul><li><b>Goods receipt:</b> add material to stock or book a direct delivery to a customer/project.</li><li><b>Issue:</b> assign consumed material to a project.</li><li><b>Return:</b> return unused project material to stock.</li><li><b>Inventory count:</b> compare counted quantities with the system and record adjustments.</li></ul><div class="erp-doc-box"><b>Important:</b> Check quantity, unit and destination before posting a movement. Corrections should remain traceable rather than hiding the original business event.</div></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="reports"><h2>9. Reports</h2><p>Reports document work performed for a customer. Add activities, working time, materials and relevant notes, then obtain the customer's signature where required.</p><p>Signed reports can be generated as PDFs and stored with the project. Review the content before finalizing because signed business documents should remain reproducible.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="files"><h2>10. Documents & photos</h2><p>Project documents and photos are stored through Nextcloud. Use project files to keep drawings, correspondence, delivery documents and site photos with the job.</p><p>Access follows the user's permissions. Do not use public links for confidential material unless the business process explicitly requires them and the link is protected appropriately.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="mobile"><h2>11. Betrio Mobile</h2><p>Betrio Mobile is designed for field use. Employees can access released projects, record time and material, work with reports and use project documents according to their permissions.</p><p>Use an individual account on every device. Test camera access, file access and the mobile browser before the first production job.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="pwa"><h2>12. Install Betrio as an app</h2><p>On supported browsers, Betrio can be installed as a Progressive Web App. Open the mobile view over HTTPS and use the browser's <b>Install app</b> or <b>Add to Home Screen</b> function.</p><p>If installation is not offered, check HTTPS, browser support and whether the application is already installed.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="offline"><h2>13. Offline work & synchronization</h2><p>Offline-capable functions cache the information required for supported mobile workflows. Synchronize before leaving a reliable network and again when connectivity returns.</p><p>Do not assume every Nextcloud or Betrio function is available offline. Verify synchronization status before relying on newly entered data on another device.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="security"><h2>14. Permissions & security</h2><p>Betrio combines Nextcloud authentication with Betrio roles and project permissions. Use least-privilege access, individual accounts and secure Nextcloud authentication.</p><ul><li>Use HTTPS for all external and mobile access.</li><li>Keep Nextcloud, PHP and Betrio updated.</li><li>Use strong passwords and multi-factor authentication where available.</li><li>Remove access promptly when an employee leaves.</li><li>Review administrative roles regularly.</li></ul></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="backup"><h2>15. Backup & updates</h2><p>Betrio's backup function protects Betrio application data. It does not replace a complete Nextcloud/server backup. Maintain regular backups of the database, Nextcloud data directory, configuration and application files.</p><p>Before updates, create a current backup and verify that recovery is possible. Test important workflows after an update before broad production use.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="security-details"><h2>Security & permissions before rollout</h2><p>Before adding all employees, test with a normal non-administrator account. Verify that the user sees only the intended modules, projects and documents and cannot reach administrative functions.</p><p>Also verify mobile logout, device locking and the procedure for lost or replaced devices.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="release-support"><h2>Version, support & updates</h2><p>The installed Betrio version is shown in the application information. When reporting a problem, include the Betrio version, Nextcloud version, PHP version, the affected module and reproducible steps.</p><p>Use the diagnostic report from System Check when technical details are needed. Review it before sharing it outside your organization.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="finanzen"><h2>Finance & accounting documents</h2><p>The finance area provides an operational overview of quotes, orders, invoices, payments and accounting-related documents. Depending on the edition and configuration, exports such as DATEV may be available.</p><p>Betrio supports the business workflow but does not replace professional tax or legal advice. Configure tax rates, numbering and invoice data according to the requirements applicable to your business.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="deinstall"><h2>Backup, restore & uninstall</h2><p>Create and verify a current backup before uninstalling Betrio. Application removal and data deletion are separate decisions: do not delete business data merely because the app is temporarily disabled.</p><p>For a migration or restore, use a compatible Betrio version and verify customers, projects, reports and generated documents after recovery.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="faq"><h2>16. Troubleshooting / FAQ</h2><h3>A user is missing in Betrio</h3><p>Make sure the Nextcloud account exists and the user has signed in at least once.</p><h3>The mobile app cannot access the camera</h3><p>Check HTTPS and the browser or operating-system permission for the camera.</p><h3>A project is not visible to a field worker</h3><p>Check project assignment, the user's Betrio role and project permissions.</p><h3>Synchronization does not update data</h3><p>Check network connectivity, Nextcloud availability and the relevant integration status before repeating the operation.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="roles"><h2>Roles & permissions – practical overview</h2><p>Administrators manage configuration and broad access. Office/project-management roles handle customers, projects and commercial workflows. Field workers receive the operational access required for assigned projects. Time-tracking-only access should remain limited to time functions.</p><div class="erp-doc-box"><b>Rule:</b> Assign the smallest role that still allows the employee to complete their work.</div></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="workflow"><h2>The complete job – from customer to archive</h2><ol><li>Create or import the customer.</li><li>Record the enquiry and schedule a site visit or measurement.</li><li>Calculate and prepare the quote.</li><li>Follow up the quote and convert an accepted quote into an order.</li><li>Prepare the work, staff, material and documents.</li><li>Record project time, material and reports during execution.</li><li>Review reports and project costs.</li><li>Prepare and issue the invoice.</li><li>Record payment and complete the project.</li><li>Keep the project record and documents according to your retention requirements.</li></ol></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="nextcloud"><h2>Working with Nextcloud</h2><p>Betrio uses native Nextcloud services where appropriate, including users, files, contacts and calendars. The selected Nextcloud calendar remains the leading calendar source for team-calendar integration.</p><p>If an integration fails, check the corresponding Nextcloud app and permissions first, then use Betrio's integration/system check.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="documents"><h2>Document management</h2><p>The document inbox collects incoming documents for review and assignment. Automatic analysis may prefill recognized values, but users should verify them before final assignment.</p><p>Possible duplicates are flagged using file information/checksums. Review the existing document before creating another record. Documents can be linked to customers, projects, suppliers and purchasing processes where supported.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="billing"><h2>Evaluation & billing</h2><p>Use evaluations to review working time and material by customer, project and employee. Billing preparation helps identify completed work that is ready for invoicing.</p><p>Before finalizing an invoice, verify recipient data, service dates, tax treatment, payment terms and the underlying project/report information.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="calendar"><h2>Team calendar</h2><p>Calendar events can be assigned to a customer, project and employee. Betrio synchronizes with the selected Nextcloud calendar according to the configured integration.</p><p>When troubleshooting, verify the selected calendar, synchronization status and whether the Nextcloud user has access to that calendar.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="system"><h2>Integration & system check</h2><p>System Check verifies important technical prerequisites and integrations. Use it after installation, after infrastructure changes and when diagnosing unexpected behavior.</p><p>The downloadable diagnostic report is designed for support and intentionally avoids passwords, tokens and customer/project content.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="device-security"><h2>Mobile security & lost devices</h2><p>Protect mobile devices with a device lock and individual Nextcloud credentials. If a device is lost, revoke sessions and access in Nextcloud and change credentials when appropriate.</p><p>Do not store shared passwords in browsers or notes. Review access when devices change owners.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="restore"><h2>Backup & restore – administrator</h2><p>Betrio backups are intended for recovery of Betrio data. Restore only a backup that matches the expected application version and environment. A safety backup should be created before every restore.</p><p>After restoring, verify record counts and test representative customers, projects, reports and documents before returning the system to normal use.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="updates"><h2>Versions & updates</h2><p>Back up the current working installation before an update. Install the new version, run the required Nextcloud upgrade and verify the registered Betrio version.</p><p>Afterwards, test login, dashboard, customers, projects, time tracking, reports, documents, finance and mobile access. Do not ignore new schema or integrity warnings without understanding their cause.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="mobilefaq"><h2>Mobile FAQ</h2><h3>The app is not offered for installation</h3><p>Use HTTPS and a supported browser. Remove an old installation if the browser believes the app is already installed.</p><h3>Photos or barcode scanning do not work</h3><p>Check camera permissions for the site/app and verify that the browser is allowed to access the camera.</p><h3>Changes are missing on another device</h3><p>Confirm that the device is online and synchronization has completed.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="support"><h2>Support & reporting errors</h2><p>For useful support requests, describe what you expected, what happened instead and the exact steps needed to reproduce it. Include version information and the System Check diagnostic report when relevant.</p><p>Do not send passwords, license secrets, authentication tokens or unnecessary customer data.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="privacy"><h2>17. Privacy</h2><p>Betrio processes business and employee data inside the connected Nextcloud environment. Your organization remains responsible for appropriate access controls, retention periods, legal bases and information obligations.</p><p>Only collect data required for the business process and restrict access to authorized users.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="about"><h2>18. About Betrio</h2><p>Betrio is a practical ERP application for trades and crafts businesses, built directly on Nextcloud. Its goal is to keep operational project work, time, material, reports, documents and commercial workflows together without forcing teams into disconnected systems.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="stores"><h2>19. Mobile apps & known app stores</h2><p>Use only official Betrio distribution channels and store listings linked by the project. Before installing a mobile build, verify the publisher and version.</p><p>The installable web app remains available through a compatible browser where supported.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="offers-calculation"><h2>Quotes & internal calculation</h2><p>Quotes combine customer-facing items with the information required for internal calculation. Keep internal costs separate from text intended for the customer.</p><p>Review quantities, units, prices, alternatives, tax and payment terms before sending the quote. Accepted quotes can be transferred into the order workflow.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="project-controlling"><h2>Project controlling & post-calculation</h2><p>Project controlling compares planned/commercial values with recorded time, material and other project costs. Use it during the project, not only after completion, so deviations can still be acted on.</p><p>Post-calculation should use complete time and material records and should be reviewed before the project is finally closed.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="smart-inbox"><h2>Smart Inbox & incoming documents</h2><p>Drop incoming business documents into the inbox for analysis and assignment. Betrio can identify document information and suggest links, but recognized values must be checked before they become part of the business record.</p><p>Use statuses such as not reviewed, needs decision, assigned and archived to keep the work queue clear.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="supplier-cockpit"><h2>Suppliers & goods receipt</h2><p>The supplier cockpit connects suppliers, purchase orders, order confirmations, expected delivery dates, delivery notes and goods receipt. Keep supplier customer numbers and conditions in the supplier master where applicable.</p><p>When goods arrive, record whether material goes into inventory or directly to a customer/project so stock and project costs remain understandable.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="invoice-35a"><h2>Labour costs under § 35a EStG</h2><p>For German private-customer invoices, Betrio can support the separate presentation of eligible labour-related amounts where configured. The correct tax/legal treatment depends on the specific case.</p><div class="erp-doc-box"><b>Note:</b> Software output is not tax advice. Have the wording and allocation used by your business checked by your tax adviser when necessary.</div></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="datev"><h2>DATEV export</h2><p>Where available in the active edition, DATEV export prepares accounting data for transfer to the tax/accounting workflow. Check account assignments, dates, tax codes and completeness before exporting.</p><p>The export is a hand-off format; final accounting treatment remains the responsibility of the accounting/tax process.</p></section>
<section class="erp-doc-section" id="project-close"><h2>Project completion</h2><p>Before closing a project, verify that time, material, reports, documents and commercial processing are complete. Check open reports and billing items and perform the post-calculation if required.</p><p>Closing a project should mark the operational end of the job without destroying its history. Keep the project record available for later reference according to your retention requirements.</p></section>
